marie: GIC-400 (GICv2) backend for the Kirin 710

Huawei P30 Lite: memory-mapped GICv2 CPU interface instead of GICv3
system registers. TrustZone owns Group 0; the virtual timer (INTID 27) and
SGI1 are non-secure Group 1 IRQs, as the milestone 0 shim measured. GICv2
SGIs target CPU interfaces (GICD_ITARGETSR0, banked), and GICC_IAR carries
the SGI source CPU in bits 12:10, so sleh_irq masks the INTID to 10 bits.

